User Interface Objects
Display and User Interface Objects
Plant Simulation provides display objects to show the results of the simulation runs and user interface
objects prompting input from the user of the simulation model.
User Interface Objects
11-4552 Plant Simulation Help
Unpublished work. © 2026 Siemens

You can:
• Use the object Button 
  for showing a button in the Frame. When you click the button, it executes the
action which you programmed in a control.
Display and User Interface Objects
Plant Simulation Help 11-4553
Unpublished work. © 2026 Siemens

• Use the object Chart 
  for presenting current data and results of the simulation run.
• Use the object Checkbox 
  for toggling between the states on and off, for toggling operating modes,
etc.
• Use the object Comment 
  for showing explanatory notes which you added to your simulation model.
• Use the object CostAnalyzer 
  for analyzing costs that the individual machines and the Worker cause.
• Use the object Dialog 
  for designing a dialog box for an object which is similar to the built-in dialog
boxes.
• Use the object Display 
  for presenting current data and results of the simulation run.
• Use the object DropDownList 
  for showing a drop-down list in the Frame. When you select one of the
items, it executes the action which you programmed in the control.
• Use the object GanttChart 
  for showing the chronological sequence of activities as bars on the time
axis.
• Use the object HtmlReport 
  for presenting current data and results of the simulation run in a report
that you can share with co-workers and customers.
• Use the object SankeyDiagram 
  for visualizing the Sankey flows of parts as well as Sankey flows of
Workers, who walk freely within the area or walk on FootPaths.
Comment
Comment [object]
Use the object Comment for showing explanatory notes which you added to your simulation model.
Image
Description
A comment helps you and your colleagues to better understand the intentions behind your model and
how it is supposed to work.
You can access it like you do any other object, be aware though that the Comment usually is not involved
in the simulation itself. Select Options > Show Comments on the View ribbon tab of the Frame or click
 to display all Comment objects, which you inserted into that Frame. Plant Simulation displays the text
in the Frame window which you entered under Display > Text.
